# Data Layer

## Room Database

Room 2.8.4 + sqliteBundled in `:shared:core-database`. Entities and DAOs live there. `ResideTrackDatabase` is the single DB instance.

- Entities: `@Entity` classes with `@ColumnInfo`. No domain logic.
- DAOs: `@Dao` with `suspend fun` or `Flow<T>` for live queries.
- `core-rooms` and other modules consume DAOs — they don't depend on entity classes beyond the DAO boundary.

## Repository Contract

Repositories expose `suspend fun (): Result<T>` (one-shot). Use `Flow<T>` only when a feature genuinely observes a live stream.

Canonical pattern (reference: `RoomsRepositoryImpl`):

```kotlin
override suspend fun getRooms(): Result<List<Room>> = withContext(dispatchers.io) {
    coRunCatching(
        tryBlock = { dao.getAll().map { it.toDomain() } },
        catchBlock = { throwable ->
            Napier.e(throwable = throwable, message = "RoomsRepositoryImpl.getRooms failed")
            throwable.wrapResultFailure()
        }
    )
}
```

Rules:
- `coRunCatching(tryBlock, catchBlock)` from `common/utils/CoroutineUtils.kt` — NOT `runCatching`, NOT bare `try/catch`.
- `wrapSuccess()` / `Throwable.wrapResultFailure()` from `common/utils/CommonUtils.kt`.
- `Napier.e(throwable) { "..." }` in catchBlock — always.
- Repositories NEVER throw to the caller — wrap everything in `Result.failure`.
- `withContext(dispatchers.io)` for DB and IO work.

## Dispatchers

`CoroutineDispatchers` (interface in `:shared:common`) is the ONLY way to get dispatchers in `commonMain` — inject it. Never reference `Dispatchers.IO` / `Dispatchers.Default` directly in `commonMain`.

Exception: platform-leaf code (Compose `actual` pickers, `androidMain` readers) may use raw `Dispatchers.IO` where Koin injection is unavailable (e.g. `AndroidFileResourceReader`). Prefer the top-level `ioDispatcher`/`defaultDispatcher` properties from `common/coroutines/Dispatchers.kt` over raw when possible.

Tests: inject a custom `CoroutineDispatchers` backed by `UnconfinedTestDispatcher`.

## DTO vs Domain

| Layer | Location | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| DB entity | `core-database/entities/` | Wire format for Room (storage shape) |
| Domain model | `core-rooms/domain/models/` or `core-domain/` | Domain shape consumed by features |

- Entity → domain mapping is the repository's responsibility.
- Domain models contain no Room annotations.
- Everything outside the repository sees only domain types.

## Mappers

- DB → domain: free-standing `internal fun XxxEntity.toDomain(): DomainType` colocated with the repository or in a `mappers/` file alongside entities.
- UI-state mappers (`Store.State/Label → Ui*State/Ui*Label`) under `<feature>/presentation/mappers/` as interface + `internal class Impl`, bound in `<feature>/impl/di/` with `singleOf<I>(::Impl)`.
